<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<specimen name="Arabidopsis">
    <view name="all" class="" db="at_root_rs" img="at_root_template_shahan.svg">
        <webservice>//bar.utoronto.ca/eplant/cgi-bin/plantefp.cgi?datasource=at_root_rs&amp;</webservice>
        <info>
            <li>MVP prototype: tissue geometry &amp; ids from the Shahan et al. (2022) root eFP SVG template; expression values pulled live from the existing <b>at_root_rs</b> eFP datasource so colouring works before final curation is confirmed by the lab.</li>
            <li>Single-cell RNA-seq atlas of the <i>Arabidopsis thaliana</i> root, comparing wild-type (Col-0) with the ground-tissue patterning mutants <i>scarecrow-4</i> (scr-4, Landsberg background backcrossed to Col-0 ×5) and <i>shortroot-2</i> (shr-2, Col-0 background).</li>
            <li>Plants were grown vertically on 1X LS, 1% sucrose plates under 16h light / 8h dark at 22°C; roots were protoplasted and profiled with the 10x Genomics Chromium Single Cell 3’ GEM Kit v3 (Illumina NovaSeq 6000).</li>
            <li>Raw and processed data deposited as GSE152766 (Shahan, Hsu, Nolan et al. 2022); processed with COPILOT (github.com/Hsu-Che-Wei/COPILOT) and integrated per-genotype as rc.integrated_scr / rc.integrated_shr Seurat objects.</li>
            <li>Cell types identified: Root cortex, Root endodermis, Pericycle, Phloem, Root procambium, Trichoblast (root-hair cell), Atrichoblast (non-hair cell), Xylem, Collumella root cap, Lateral root cap, Vascular bundle, Xylem pole pericycle, Protoxylem, Phloem pole pericycle, and Metaxylem.</li>
            <li><b>Sample assignment note for Vincent to verify:</b> GSE152766 contains 2 scr-4 samples (sc_25/GSM4626000, sc_36/GSM4626003) and 2 shr-2 samples (sc_52/GSM4626007, sc_53/GSM4626008), each with its own GEO-annotated batch-matched wild-type controls (sc_20/sc_21 for the scr-4 batch; sc_30/sc_31 for the other scr-4 batch; sc_51 for the shr-2 batch). The Col-0 tissue entries below use the union of these five batch-matched WT samples (GSM4625998, GSM4625999, GSM4626001, GSM4626002, GSM4626006) as the wild-type baseline shown alongside both mutants, rather than the full 15-sample WT pool used to build the main root atlas — please confirm this is the right baseline before this goes live.</li>
            <li>Results from Shahan, Hsu, Nolan et al. (2022) <i>Developmental Cell</i> 57(4):543-560.e9. DOI: 10.1016/j.devcel.2022.01.008</li>
        </info>

